scale-to-width-down/40?cb=20110203234631\" /></a></span>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th></tr>\n<tr style=\"height:40px; text-align:center\">\n<th bgcolor=\"068FB0\">4\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\">&#160;\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\">&#160;\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\">&#160;\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\">&#160;\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th></tr>\n<tr style=\"height:40px; text-align:center\">\n<th bgcolor=\"068FB0\">5\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\">&#160;\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\"><span typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/5/58/DFF_Hard_Battle_Piece.png/revision/latest?cb=20110203235357\" class=\"mw-file-description image\" title=\"Imaginary Brawler\"><img alt=\"Imaginary Brawler\"  decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"33\" height=\"40\" class=\"mw-file-element lazyload\" data-image-name=\"DFF Hard Battle Piece.png\" data-image-key=\"DFF_Hard_Battle_Piece.png\" data-relevant=\"1\" src=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/5/58/DFF_Hard_Battle_Piece.png/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/33?cb=20110203235357\" /></a></span>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th></tr>\n<tr style=\"height:40px; text-align:center\">\n<th bgcolor=\"068FB0\">6\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\"><span typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/f/fc/DFF_Potion.png/revision/latest?cb=20110203235732\" class=\"mw-file-description image\" title=\"Potion\"><img alt=\"Potion\"  decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"21\" height=\"40\" class=\"mw-file-element lazyload\" data-image-name=\"DFF Potion.png\" data-image-key=\"DFF_Potion.png\" data-relevant=\"1\" src=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/f/fc/DFF_Potion.png/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/21?cb=20110203235732\" /></a></span>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th></tr>\n<tr style=\"height:40px; text-align:center\">\n<th bgcolor=\"068FB0\">7\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th></tr></tbody></table>\n<p>Behind the Stalwart is a chest with a BRV Zero skill, guess what it does to enemies in chains. Only at the start, not for the whole match. Only the next gateway now.\n</p><p>Guess where we use the Straight Chain I told you to buy, go on, guess. We're up against a Fleeting Flash with Leviathan, a Delusory Dragoon, two Imaginary Brawlers both with Bahamut, and the Ephemeral Summon at A2 who isn't part of the chain. The Expert Battle Piece at E3 is a Fallacious Tree, and this one has Turn Guard, Omni Block, and Reverse Polarity so watch out. It has two Muscle Belts and a 2.9x multiplier when close to you, and after 45 seconds pass another booster triggers to double that booster to 5.9 (boosters track the decimals beyond the first one but don't round up, so it's actually 2.98, which is why it doubles to 5.9). Exdeath only has one physical attack, Sword Dance, but that <i>is</i> one of his potential counters so if you get blocked, you are going to experience a lot of pain with those boosters pumping up the Sword Dance counters, and again, since you're staggering from being blocked, he has a higher critical hit ratio during the counters. And to top it off, he has the Cactuar summon. Use the fights before him to build up your EX Gauge to help on him, then use the Potion to recharge it for the boss. Remember Tifa does more damage the most EX she has, so if you want to do her EX Burst on the Tree enter EX Mode in the middle of her HP attack so she has the most possible EX and the Burst is its strongest potential.\n</p><p>During this round of fights Tifa learned Falcon's Dive and Rolling Blaze. So Jecht has Falcon Punch, Prishe has Falcon Kick, I guess Tifa got the leftovers. It's a downward diving kick of course, its pretty good for its utility in well, being a diving attack. Rolling Blaze is a forward and down rolling attack, it does a keen bit of Bravery damage too. The chest has Metal Knuckles for us, nowhere near as powerful as the Snowscepter.\n</p>\n<table style=\"width: 275px; D012 article-table; text-align: center; color:black; float:right\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"font-size: larger; background:#1E90FF\" colspan=\"6\"><font color=\"white\"><b>Boss</b></font>\n</td></tr>\n<tr bgcolor=\"#1E90FF\">\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\" colspan=\"6\"><b><a href=\"https://finalfantasy.fandom.com/wiki/Ultimecia_(Dissidia_PSP)\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" title=\"Ultimecia (Dissidia PSP)\">Ultimecia</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr bgcolor=\"#dddddd\">\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\" colspan=\"6\"><span typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/9/9b/UltimeciaDissidiaRender.PNG/revision/latest?cb=20110822193930\" class=\"mw-file-description image\"><img alt=\"UltimeciaDissidiaRender\"  decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"100\" height=\"126\" class=\"mw-file-element lazyload\" data-image-name=\"UltimeciaDissidiaRender.PNG\" data-image-key=\"UltimeciaDissidiaRender.PNG\" data-relevant=\"1\" src=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/9/9b/UltimeciaDissidiaRender.PNG/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/100?cb=20110822193930\" /></a></span>\n</td></tr>\n<tr bgcolor=\"#1E90FF\">\n<td width=\"33%\" colspan=\"2\"><b>HP</b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"33%\" colspan=\"2\"><b>Level</b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"33%\" colspan=\"2\"><b>Bravery</b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr bgcolor=\"#dddddd\">\n<td colspan=\"2\">2,422\n</td>\n<td colspan=\"2\">12\n</td>\n<td colspan=\"2\">253\n</td></tr>\n<tr bgcolor=\"#1E90FF\">\n<td colspan=\"6\"><b>Brave Attacks</b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr bgcolor=\"#dddddd\">\n<td colspan=\"6\">Knight's Blade, Knight's Axe, Knight's Spear, Knight's Arrow\n</td></tr>\n<tr bgcolor=\"#1E90FF\">\n<td colspan=\"6\"><b>HP Attacks</b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr bgcolor=\"#dddddd\">\n<td colspan=\"6\">Shockwave Pulsar, Apocalypse\n</td></tr>\n<tr bgcolor=\"#1E90FF\">\n<td colspan=\"3\"><b>Summon</b>\n</td>\n<td colspan=\"3\"><b>Difficulty</b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr bgcolor=\"#dddddd\">\n<td colspan=\"3\">Calcabrina\n</td>\n<td colspan=\"3\">1/5\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p>Confront the end piece to find Ultimecia, the only other cast member with a character and personality as bland and unexplored as Tifa's. Okay, others are bland, but their confrontations have purpose, Cloud of Darkness has an awesome VA and shows some interesting insights on her thoughts about manikins at least. Ultimecia just says \"I'm bored, was looking for someone to fight, you'll do\". How exciting, the game doesn't even pretend to have a reason for this fight, it just needs a boss to throw at us.\n</p><p>Ultimecia is a boss that's difficult only on paper. The \"difficult on paper\" is that she's an long-range aerial character, fighting in an aerial arena, and Tifa is a melee fighter with crappy aerial attacks at this point of the game. The Calcabrina summon removes Break status from us, sounds meh, until you realize it also stops the normal Bravery regen that occurs when we're Broken, so we're stuck at 7 Bravery and can be Broken again easily. She also has an Attractorb, Pearl Necklace, and a Far from Opponent and EX Mode boosters. They don't give much though.\n</p><p>The reason the difficulty is only on paper is because she has <i>three Cursed Rings</i>. Yeah, those accessories that sap defense by 50%, usually worn by manikins? She has three. I started off with a Beat Rush, Broke her, got a Bravery boost from Ifrit, entered EX Mode as I entered Chase, and an HP attack wall rushed her and put her at 200 HP as I began the EX Burst. What an anti-climax this fight is, Ultimecia is a total pushover, you should have no trouble crushing her. I'm almost wondering if this is a glitch, only two boosters and not even good ones, maybe they meant to give her three more boosters and accidentally gave her Cursed Rings? Who knows.\n</p><p>After the battle Tifa runs up to kick Ultimecia, but she turns out to be a manikin. Hm, guess that explains the Cursed Rings. The real Ultimecia prepares to strike Tifa from behind. Suddenly Kain arrives and saves the day. Ultimecia taunts that she'd worry about Kain as an attacker than a savior, and points out a fallen Zidane who has appeared from nowhere, and says Kain attacked him. Tifa believes her for some reason and goes after Kain when he grabs Zidane and takes off.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"The_Chase\">The Chase</span><a title=\"Edit section&#39;s source code: The Chase\" data-tracking-label=\"edit-section-anon\" data-action=\"edit-section\" href=\"https://finalfantasy.fandom.com/wiki/Walkthrough:Dissidia_012_Final_Fantasy/Drake/Part_7?action=edit&amp;section=3\" aria-label=\"Edit section&#39;s source code: The Chase\"><svg class=\"wds-icon wds-icon-tiny\" aria-hidden=\"true\" focusable=\"false\"><use xlink:href=\"#wds-icons-pencil-tiny\"></use></svg></a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"D012 board\" style=\"float:right\">\n\n<tbody><tr bgcolor=\"068FB0\">\n<td width=\"19px;background:white\">&#160;\n</td>\n<th style=\"width:40px\">A\n</th>\n<th style=\"width:40px\">B\n</th>\n<th style=\"width:40px\">C\n</th>\n<th style=\"width:40px\">D\n</th>\n<th style=\"width:40px\">E\n</th>\n<th style=\"width:40px\">F\n</th>\n<th style=\"width:40px\">G\n</th>\n<th style=\"width:40px\">H\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th></tr>\n<tr style=\"height:40px; text-align:cen